# QuickNotes REST API Design

## 1. Overview

QuickNotes is a note-management service that allows authenticated
users to create, retrieve, update, and delete notes and organize
them with tags.

Base URL:

`https://api.quicknotes.example.com/v1`

The hostname is illustrative and must be replaced with the production
API hostname before deployment.

Content type: `application/json`

Authentication: Bearer access token.

Example header:

`Authorization: Bearer <access-token>`

## 2. REST endpoints

| Method | Path | Description | Success status |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/auth/register` | Register a new user | 201 Created |
| POST | `/auth/login` | Authenticate and issue tokens | 200 OK |
| GET | `/notes` | List the authenticated user's notes | 200 OK |
| POST | `/notes` | Create a note | 201 Created |
| GET | `/notes/{noteId}` | Retrieve one note | 200 OK |
| PATCH | `/notes/{noteId}` | Update selected note fields | 200 OK |
| DELETE | `/notes/{noteId}` | Delete a note | 204 No Content |
| GET | `/tags` | List the user's tags | 200 OK |
| POST | `/tags` | Create a tag | 201 Created |
| PUT | `/notes/{noteId}/tags/{tagId}` | Attach a tag to a note | 204 No Content |
| DELETE | `/notes/{noteId}/tags/{tagId}` | Detach a tag from a note | 204 No Content |

All note and tag endpoints require authentication, except registration
and login.

The API must scope every note and tag query to the authenticated user.
Knowing another user's resource ID must not grant access to that resource.

## 3. List notes

### Request

`GET /v1/notes?limit=10&cursor=`

Headers:

`Authorization: Bearer <access-token>`

Optional query parameters:

- `limit`: number of records per page, from 1 to 100.
- `cursor`: opaque pagination cursor returned by the previous response.
- `tagId`: return notes associated with a particular tag.

### Successful response: 200 OK

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "note_101",
      "title": "Business ideas",
      "body": "Research customer problems before building.",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-24T10:00:00Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-24T10:00:00Z",
      "tags": [
        {
          "id": "tag_5",
          "name": "Business"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "pagination": {
    "limit": 10,
    "nextCursor": null
  }
}
